title ALES177 — Lotus's stereo_ring_mod: the ring modulator (bipolar triangle carrier on amplitude) carried into stereo, the SAME carrier on BOTH channels — the second rung of the stereo MODULATION class, the tremolo's sibling
prompt Autonomous loop lap after ALES176: take the next agent-doable crux Lindy-first crux-first, self-approve the design round, send each finished increment to origin and xykj61 as its own signed round, STOP at custody gates.
think ALES176 opened the stereo modulation class with the tremolo (carrier held to an attenuation, never crossing zero). Crux-first within the class: its named sibling the ring modulator (ALES75) is the same thin per-sample rung with ONE bound widened — the bipolar carrier may cross zero and flip the sample's sign, scattering the spectrum into metallic sum-and-difference tones. A ring modulator whose carrier never goes negative is EXACTLY the tremolo, so it is the natural second rung and it binds directly to ALES176.
think Composed stereo_ring_mod mirroring stereo_tremolo: StereoRingModError = ring_mod.RingModError reused whole; validate ONCE up front. ring_mod's four checks were inline, so factored them into a shared pub precheck (mirroring the ALES176 tremolo refactor and tone.precheck) and had mono ring_mod call it; the mono ales_ring_mod_witness re-runs GREEN. Carried the honest asymmetric-rail subtlety: −32768·−1 = 32768 saturates to 32767 per channel, the one place the ring modulator's saturate earns its keep unlike the tremolo's no-op.
think Proved four laws: stereo ring law (each channel == mono ring_mod byte for byte, channels genuinely differing); tremolo-sibling law (a non-negative carrier == ALES176's stereo tremolo on both proven by running tremolo.tremolo per channel, a bipolar carrier genuinely diverging); image law (identical-channel master stays identical AND a right-is-half-left pan keeps its L:R ratio sample for sample THROUGH the sign flips — both sides times the same c(k)); balance/silence/atomicity/degenerate (four refusals — BadPeriod, BadDepth, BadCarrier, BadRange — each leaving both channels untouched and balanced, count 0 the identity).
obs No custody gate reached — pure local i16 DSP siloed to lotus/, a self-approved design round. Built and ran on metal; witness GREEN through Rishi, TAME clean (opening triad, ≥2 asserts/fn with // invariant, no @memcpy, named errors with try, triangle+multiply in i64, saturate honest at the lone corner), width exit 0. The stereo modulation class now holds tremolo and ring modulator (the amplitude pair); the next rungs carry the delay-line modulations (chorus, vibrato, flanger — each channel keeping its own delay-line snapshot) or auto_pan.
loom witness=ales_stereo_ring_mod_witness selftest=GREEN laws=4 channels=2 class=modulation-rung-2
